diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 7fcd5ab..708de26 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -5,5 +5,16 @@ A small library that ships application log records to the log collector.
 - `Record::make()` builds a record. The text is cut at 16 KiB, and control characters become spaces.
 - `AsyncSink` queues records and writes them in batches on its own worker thread through a `Transport`.
 - `SinkRegistry` names the sinks of a process and counts their dropped records for the metrics page.
+- `toJsonLine()` encodes a record as one JSON Lines entry for the collector.
 
-A full queue refuses new records: `push()` returns false.
+## Full queue
+
+A full queue keeps the newest records: `push()` drops the oldest queued record and counts it in `SinkRegistry::drops()`. Before this version, `push()` refused the new record, and the newest lines of an incident were lost.
+
+## Batches
+
+A batch holds at most `SinkOptions::maxBatchBytes` of text (256 KiB by default), so the collector never sees a request above its limit.
+
+## Shutdown
+
+Call `flush()` in the shutdown hook to wait until the transport has each queued record, then `close()`.
